* Zama FHEVM architecture
** Two ideas
*** Symbolic execution: chain derives handles, emits events
*** Threshold decryption: one global key, secret-shared
** Six components
*** FHEVM Solidity library
*** Host contracts: Executor, ACL, InputVerifier, KMSVerifier, HCULimit
*** Coprocessors (TFHE-rs, evaluation key)
*** Gateway (Arbitrum rollup, coordination contracts)
*** KMS (13 MPC nodes, Nitro Enclaves)
*** Relayer and oracle (untrusted edge)
** Three keys
*** Public key: client encrypts
*** Evaluation key: coprocessors compute
*** Private key: shared across the KMS
** Life of a value
*** Encrypt + ZKPoK on the device
*** Coprocessor attestation (inputProof)
*** InputVerifier: threshold of signatures
*** Executor: handle = hash(op, inputs, block)
*** Off-chain evaluation + ciphertext commitment
*** Public or user decryption via Gateway and KMS
** Access control
*** Persistent, transient, public decryption
*** Checked at use and at read
*** Never revoked; new handle per operation
*** Replicated to the Gateway, enforced by the KMS
** Trust model
*** Host contracts: audited, upgradeable
*** Coprocessors: honest majority, staking, slashing
*** Gateway: liveness only
*** KMS: 2/3 of 13 + enclaves
*** Correctness attested, not proven (ZK-FHE later)
